  "body": "Part of #866.\n\n**What the reporter saw:** a log line `gpu: slow frame 35098 ms ... slowest phase \"commands\" 35097 ms` right after importing a STEP, read as a 35-second UI freeze.\n\n**Root cause:** the native file dialogs (`crates/ui/src/file_dialog.rs`, rfd) are modal and synchronous, and they are opened from `State::drain_actions`, inside the frame's \"commands\" phase (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell_window/frame.rs`). The frame watch (`frame_watch.rs`, #74) therefore counted the time the user spent browsing for the file as app work. The log's xdg-desktop-portal warning (the dialog opening) sits right before the slow frame. The STEP itself tessellates off-thread as before; no command ran for 35 s.\n\n**Fix:** the dialog seam times every modal dialog (`file_dialog::take_waited`), and the frame watch takes that time off the frame it happened in (`FrameWatch::excuse`), so a slow frame names real work only.\n\n**Done means:** time spent in a modal file dialog never shows up as a slow \"commands\" frame, and real work beyond it still does - pinned by `frame_watch::tests::time_in_a_modal_dialog_is_not_a_slow_frame`.\n\n(Not in scope: making the file dialogs asynchronous so the window keeps repainting behind them - the usual modal behaviour, separate if wanted.)\n",
